course: dictionary
lesson: 3153
title: Words that paint a picture
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: Some words name a thing, and some words name a colour. Emerald can be both. An emerald is a bright green precious stone, and emerald is also the bright, rich green colour of that stone. Context tells you which one is meant. «The ring had a shining emerald set in gold.» Here it is a stone, because a ring can hold a jewel.
explain: «The hills were a deep emerald after the spring rain.» Hills cannot be stones, so emerald must be describing a colour. Ask yourself: is this sentence describing a thing, or how something looks? That question helps you choose the right meaning.
explain: Emerald can also be part of a nickname. The Emerald Isle is a name for Ireland, because of its green fields. A place name with capital letters is a clue that the word is a proper name, not a stone.
fact: An emerald is a bright green precious stone used in jewellery.
fact: Emerald is a bright, rich green colour.
fact: «Emeralds are green beryl, and the finest came from Colombia, where the Spanish took them from the 1500s.» Emeralds belong to the beryl family of minerals.
fact: The Emerald Isle is a nickname for Ireland, because of its green fields.
fact: Emerald is a noun for the stone and the colour, and an adjective, as in «an emerald scarf».
exercise: «Emeralds are green beryl, and the finest came from Colombia.» What is an emerald in this sentence? | A bright blue sky | A kind of wooden boat | A type of small bird | *A bright green precious stone
exercise: «The hills of Ireland were a bright emerald after the rain.» What does emerald describe? | A hard grey rock | A loud noise | A warm loaf of bread | *A bright, rich green colour
exercise: What is the Emerald Isle? | A small island in the middle of a lake | A jewellery shop in London | A type of ship | *A nickname for Ireland, because of its green fields
test: «The ring had a shining emerald set in gold.» What is the emerald in this sentence? | A dog's collar | A kind of gold coin | *A stone used in jewellery | A colour of a painted door
test: «Her new coat was emerald, bright as a summer leaf.» What does emerald mean here? | A bright red | A type of cloth made of silk | A sort of hat | *A bright, rich green
exam: Why is Ireland called the Emerald Isle? | Because it is very cold | Because it has a famous gem mine | Because it is a very small island | *Because of its green fields
